                        "evidence":  [
                                         "struct ip6_frag layout (ip6.h:191-196): ip6f_nxt[0], ip6f_reserved[1], ip6f_offlg[2-3], ip6f_ident[4-7]. print-frag6.c:43 checks only ND_TCHECK(dp-\u003eip6f_offlg) covering bytes 2-3, but print-frag6.c:47 accesses EXTRACT_32BITS(\u0026dp-\u003eip6f_ident) at bytes 4-7 and print-frag6.c:49 accesses EXTRACT_16BITS(\u0026ip6-\u003eip6_plen) from bp2 without any bounds verification. Binary confirms frag6_print is compiled at offset 0x599e0 and called from ip6_print in print-ip6.c:307 for IPPROTO_FRAGMENT packets."
                                     ],
                        "raw_text":  [
                                         "{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"duration_ms\":85327,\"duration_api_ms\":85119,\"num_turns\":9,\"result\":\"The evidence is clear. The vulnerability is in `frag6_print()` in `print-frag6.c`. The function only bounds-checks `dp-\u003eip6f_offlg` (2 bytes at offset 2 of the struct) but then accesses `dp-\u003eip6f_ident` (4 bytes at offset 4) without any bounds check. A truncated packet containing exactly 4 bytes of fragment header passes the check but triggers a 4-byte over-read on `ip6f_ident`.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"predicted_cves\\\": [\\\"CVE-2017-13005\\\"],\\n  \\\"predicted_files\\\": [\\\"print-frag6.c\\\"],\\n  \\\"predicted_functions\\\": [\\\"frag6_print\\\"],\\n  \\\"root_cause\\\": \\\"Insufficient ND_TCHECK bounds check in frag6_print. Only dp-\u003eip6f_offlg (offset 2, 2 bytes) is checked via ND_TCHECK, but dp-\u003eip6f_ident (offset 4, 4 bytes) and ip6-\u003eip6_plen are accessed without corresponding bounds checks. A truncated packet with exactly 4 bytes of fragment header data (enough for ip6f_nxt + ip6f_reserved + ip6f_offlg) passes the ND_TCHECK check at offset 2 but causes a 4-byte out-of-bounds read at offset 4 when EXTRACT_32BITS(\u0026dp-\u003eip6f_ident) is evaluated.\\\",\\n  \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"struct ip6_frag layout (ip6.h:191-196): ip6f_nxt[0], ip6f_reserved[1], ip6f_offlg[2-3], ip6f_ident[4-7]. print-frag6.c:43 checks only ND_TCHECK(dp-\u003eip6f_offlg) covering bytes 2-3, but print-frag6.c:47 accesses EXTRACT_32BITS(\u0026dp-\u003eip6f_ident) at bytes 4-7 and print-frag6.c:49 accesses EXTRACT_16BITS(\u0026ip6-\u003eip6_plen) from bp2 without any bounds verification. Binary confirms frag6_print is compiled at offset 0x599e0 and called from ip6_print in print-ip6.c:307 for IPPROTO_FRAGMENT packets.\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"9e7e45c8-6f15-49cb-9d0a-4d69c4e0770b\",\"total_cost_usd\":0.271